From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:37:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: set the device up again when suspend reset the IP

Resume assumes that the IP kept its registers and restores only the
power-down bits, the interrupt enables and the pullup. On the Gemini
the SPM's mem suspend path cuts the IP's power. After resume the IPPC
reads as after a power-on reset: the IP software reset is asserted, the
U2 port is disabled and selected for the host, and every MAC register
reads zero. The U2 PHY keeps its settings. The gadget then never
enumerated again: a replug produced no interrupt, and neither a soft
disconnect and connect nor a role write recovered it, because in dual
role mode neither runs the device setup again. Suspend to idle keeps
the registers and was not affected.

At resume, when the software reset reads asserted, take the IP out of
reset and repeat the device setup that probe does: the device reset,
the port enable and selection, the CSR defaults and the speed. The
existing resume then powers the device on, enables its interrupts and
restores the pullup. A host-side setup after such a reset is not done
here.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_dr.h   |  4 ++++
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
index 5d091dc44..88a13f91c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
@@ -1030,6 +1030,26 @@ bool ssusb_gadget_ip_sleep_check(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Set the device side up again after the IP was reset with every register
+ * at its default, as probe does: the port selection, the CSRs and the
+ * speed. Resume then powers the device on, enables its interrupts and
+ * restores the pullup as usual.
+ */
+void ssusb_gadget_restore(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
+{
+	struct mtu3 *mtu = ssusb->u3d;
+
+	if (!mtu)
+		return;
+
+	mtu3_device_reset(mtu);
+	if (mtu3_device_enable(mtu))
+		dev_err(mtu->dev, "device enable failed after reset\n");
+	mtu3_regs_init(mtu);
+	mtu3_set_speed(mtu, mtu->speed);
+}
+
 int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 {
 	struct mtu3 *mtu = ssusb->u3d;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_dr.h b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_dr.h
index e325508bd..34ade5dc3 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_dr.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_dr.h
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ void ssusb_gadget_exit(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb);
 int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg);
 int ssusb_gadget_resume(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg);
 bool ssusb_gadget_ip_sleep_check(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb);
+void ssusb_gadget_restore(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb);
 
 #else
 static inline int ssusb_gadget_init(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
@@ -87,6 +88,9 @@ static inline bool ssusb_gadget_ip_sleep_check(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
 	return true;
 }
 
+static inline void ssusb_gadget_restore(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
+{}
+
 #endif
 
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
index fb88fbdb7..803bebe89 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
@@ -575,6 +575,19 @@ static int mtu3_resume_common(struct device *dev, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (ret)
 		goto phy_err;
 
+	/*
+	 * A suspend that cut the IP's power, such as the MT6797 SPM's mem
+	 * path, leaves it held in reset with every register at its default.
+	 * Take it out of reset and set the device side up again; a host
+	 * side would need its own setup, which is not done here.
+	 */
+	if (mtu3_readl(ssusb->ippc_base, U3D_SSUSB_IP_PW_CTRL0) & SSUSB_IP_SW_RST) {
+		dev_info(dev, "IP was reset in suspend, setting it up again\n");
+		ssusb_ip_sw_reset(ssusb);
+		if (!ssusb->is_host)
+			ssusb_gadget_restore(ssusb);
+	}
+
 	return resume_ip_and_ports(ssusb, msg);
 
 phy_err:
-- 
2.43.0

